      "en": "Considering scenic art as existential liturgy (completion 4), Marcel seals his grandiose vision of the spiritual role of theater. In an era tormented by the anguish of the absurd and the vertigo of technical dehumanization, the theatrical stage remains one of the rare sanctuaries where the human person can undergo the lived experience of fraternity and hope. The silence shared in the darkness of the hall weaves among the spectators a mysterious communion prefiguring the Kingdom. Thus, for Gabriel Marcel, theater is not a profane entertainment, but an authentic propaedeutic to spiritual life, a viaticum that accompanies Homo Viator journeying toward the homeland of Being."
